Z||000000||Jake_Dragon||11-28-2001||05:51 PM||||Ok I don't shop there but the wife does.<BR>She purchased a collector Barbie doll for a Christmas present, turns out the person we bought the doll for already has one.<BR>Wal-Mart will not take the doll back.<BR>There seems to be an policy against returning collector dolls, it is not posted or written on the receipt but it does seem to exist. I don't care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/left.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CHSpiff.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/right.gif">             <BR>                 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt2_3.GIF"> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-28-2001||05:59 PM||||I've always felt that Wally World's had the best return policy of any of the major department store chains.  A few years back I bought a 27" TV from them.  About a year later, lightning smoked it.  I brought it back to Wally World (without a box or receipt) and they gladly exchanged it, no questions asked.  Maybe you should try to exchange the doll for something else.<P>The only no refund policy I know of there is on music/computer media.  If a CD/cassette/CDROM/etc is opened, it's yours.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||11-28-2001||06:00 PM||||What kind of happy horsesh!t is that?! Listen, I know my way around a WalMart, believe you me, and ANYTHING can be returned if you stay in their face long enough. Just keep asking for a manager.<P>Or Plan B, Put it on Ebay and double your money. There is some Waylon P. Smithers type more money then brains hahmersessual Barbie collecter out there with an itchy Visa card.||||reg||1
