Z||000016||84Bill||11-29-2001||12:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Hey, when I used to work at K-mart (a few years back) some old witch came in with a used toaster over wanting a refund.  Normally that wouldn't be a problem, except she had no receipt, no box, this was an older model AND there were food crumbs inside.  She could've found it in the trash somewhere.<P>To my protest, we gave her a refund.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>WalMart usually takes back anything, receipt or not.  Keep trying.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I worked the home improvement department at K Mart a few years back and I had a drunken guy return a gallon of paint that was almost empty and wanted a refund because it was not the right color!!! I asked him where the paint went and he said he spilled it. I got a manager to deal with him because he was getting loud and obnoxious. Needless to say he got his money back  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000017||Black86SE||11-29-2001||07:34 PM||||yeah, sometimes it is a lot easier to return something than to deal with the customer. I work at a hardware store and I have dealt with some funny situations of people trying to return something. People who buy paint and then bring it back cause they don't like the color and expect a new gallon, no charge. WTF? I work at ACE Hardware, and this is the best. People who insist that the bought an item from my store, when the tag on the item specificaly says "Meijer". I have to point it out to them and then sometimes they get mad and storm out cause they are stupid. I love retail. (NOT!)||||reg||1
